// DRAFT (2026-11-07, vocab-tables session). Review doc: wiki/design/VOCAB_TABLES.md
//
// NOT AN INSTRUCTION TABLE. Deliberately has no "kind_categories"/"instructions" keys, so pointing
// paths.instruction_tables at it fails loudly (KeyError in parsexml._load_instruction_tables) instead of
// silently emitting "unknown concrete_instruction — skipped" markers (parsexml.py:2535-2537).
//
// Every candidate below needs an approval-gated change before it can be used:
//   emitter   = a new branch in pass5_emit_llvm (parsexml.py:2144-2537 dispatches on the concrete NAME)
//   stl_eval  = a case in _stl_arch_values (parsexml.py:1131-1168), else stl_bypass raises ValueError and skips the test
//   pass2_5   = the branch override (parsexml.py:754-836) currently forces br_bez / br_cond, so br candidates are ignored
//   marker    = the transmitting instruction must carry the __litmus_<stem>_pc<N> label: compile_annotate.py:269-281
//               uses the marker offset as xmit.addr (only br_x is re-located to the jcc). Put any prelude (zeroing,
//               flag setup) BEFORE the label, as in the scratch probe (VOCAB_TABLES.md "Emitter gaps").
// "asm" strings were compiled with clang 21 for x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu (-O2, -S and -c) in a scratch probe; they assemble.
// "defenses" = which per-defense table should carry it (VOCAB_TABLES.md has the per-defense reasons and citations).
// "sources" keys: STT=Yu 2019, SPT=Choudhary 2021, RECON=Aimoniotis 2023, INVISI=Yan 2018, CLEANUP=Saileshwar 2019,
//   SPECLFB=Cheng 2024, AMULET=Fu 2025, NDA=Weisse 2019, DOM=Sakalis 2019, DOPPEL=Kvalsvik 2023 (all PDF page numbers;
//   RECON is an HTML print so sections only); G5=local gem5-recon source copy at
//   ~/Documents/stanford/trippel/spectre-verify/run_asm/gem5-recon (path relative to src/arch/x86/isa/insts/general_purpose/).
{
  "schema": "simspect.vocab_candidates/v0-draft",
  "candidates": {
